# Gates a workflow runs that `npm run ci` deliberately does NOT run.
#
# Read by scripts/check-ci-chain-parity.ts. Entries are either a package.json
# script name (`check:ci-foo`) or a repo-relative shell path
# (`.ci/scripts/quality/check-foo.sh`), and every entry needs a BLOCKER reason
# validated by the shared blocker-validator.
#
# An exemption is a HOLE in the promise that `npm run ci` catches CI failures
# before a push. The bar is "this gate cannot run on a developer machine at
# all", not "it is slow" or "it is noisy". Everything below needs either a live
# pull request or credentials a developer does not hold.

# BLOCKER: reads the PR head/base refs from the GITHUB_* event environment and queries the GitHub API for the branch's PR; outside a pull_request event there is no branch pair to validate, so a local run has nothing to check
.ci/scripts/quality/check-branch.sh

# BLOCKER: fetches the PR's commit list over the GitHub API to assert no commit carries an unwanted Claude attribution trailer; a local checkout has no PR number and the commits are not yet pushed
.ci/scripts/quality/check-claude-attribution.sh

# BLOCKER: reads the pull request body and its updatedAt timestamp through the GitHub API to enforce the description-freshness rule; there is no PR body to read before the PR exists
.ci/scripts/quality/check-pr-description.sh

# BLOCKER: walks the PR's review threads via the GitHub GraphQL API and fails on unresolved ones; nothing about it is computable from a local working tree
.ci/scripts/quality/check-resolved-threads.sh

# BLOCKER: pulls bot review comments for the PR over the GitHub API and asserts each has a substantive reply; requires an open PR plus an authenticated token
.ci/scripts/quality/check-review-comments.sh

# BLOCKER: compares each submodule pointer against the branches open on the submodule's own GitHub remote; needs API access to three repos and a PR context to resolve the expected branch
.ci/scripts/quality/check-submodule-branches.sh

# BLOCKER: drives the Gemini review bot through the GitHub API on a live PR; it is a review orchestration step rather than a validator, and has no meaning outside a pull_request run
.ci/scripts/quality/trigger-gemini-review.sh
.ci/scripts/quality/wait-gemini-review.sh

# BLOCKER: probes the release-state sentinels in the R2 bucket, so it needs R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID/R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY; a developer without release credentials gets "Required environment variable 'R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID' is not set" rather than a verdict
.ci/scripts/quality/check-release-state.sh
